//? Title: UPGMA: actual cluster sizes and weighted merges
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Pairwise distances between taxa can be summarized by a rooted average-linkage
tree. UPGMA repeatedly joins the closest active clusters, using leaf counts to
preserve the mean pairwise distance after each merge.
)

\toc

> The method

If clusters A and B merge, d(A∪B,C)=(|A|d(A,C)+|B|d(B,C))/(|A|+|B|). Expanding
each average proves that this is the average over every leaf pair, so unequal
cluster sizes must not be weighted equally. Join height is d(A,B)/2. Every leaf
starts at height0 and root-to-leaf branch lengths telescope to root height,
giving an ultrametric output. The naive complete pair scan costs Σ_m
m(m−1)/2=O(n³); it does not estimate whether the observed data obey a molecular
clock.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/upgma_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/upgma.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::upgma({{0, 2, 6}, {2, 0, 4}, {6, 4, 0}});
    std::print("| left | right | left size | right size | actual height |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for (auto m : r.merges)
        std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|\n", m.left, m.right, m.left_size,
                   m.right_size, m.height);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Three taxa: distances2,6,4");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("First actual height {}",
                                     r.merges[0].height));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual root height {}",
                                     r.merges.back().height));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/upgma_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| left | right | left size | right size | actual height |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
|0|1|1|1|1|
|2|3|1|2|2.5|
\image(figures/upgma_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual native producing values from the complete small worked example.)
