> Interpretation and limits

Input must be square, finite, nonnegative, exactly symmetric and have zero
diagonal. Empty and singleton inputs produce no joins. The500-leaf ceiling
reflects the cubic implementation. Weighted means use widened intermediates. The
dendrogram reads actual native merges and uses iterative layout.

The complete editable C++ programs save figures locally; results contain
ordinary computed Markdown. Selected counters describe actual producer
operations, excluding validation when stated.

> References

- Sokal and Michener average-linkage method; the size-weighted recurrence and
  ultrametric construction are derived above.

